                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37fed087-af3b-3836-aeb6-2afecbfe5ac1",
                        "entry_id": "8cb9f914-56b0-3f2b-b8d5-50b21112c58b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "En Inde, paysan, cultivateur."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "aa78634d-906d-4a4b-89f1-4a889b82d2ec",
                                "sense_id": "37fed087-af3b-3836-aeb6-2afecbfe5ac1",
                                "text": "Certains de ces ryots serviles étaient hindous et appartenaient aux couches les plus pauvres de la société, mais nombre d’entre eux – la plupart – étaient musulmans."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "72f9b8c9-0196-4d1f-ad57-618255e9e3b2",
                                "sense_id": "37fed087-af3b-3836-aeb6-2afecbfe5ac1",
                                "text": "Ils constituent tout simplement la piétaille et sont bons pour être dévorés par la fièvre ; ils partagent avec le ryot et le bœuf de labour l’honneur d’être le socle sur lequel repose l’État."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b568b8d9-72c0-450b-967c-1e9cd5173466",
                        "source_entry_id": "8cb9f914-56b0-3f2b-b8d5-50b21112c58b",
                        "source_sense_id": "37fed087-af3b-3836-aeb6-2afecbfe5ac1",
                        "target_lang_word": "ryot",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ryot",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b6d0ae8-67e8-3b0a-9439-1b02e8aa8030",
                                        "entry_id": "a85de561-64fb-3e1f-b3a1-b8986ad5ab3e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A farmer or tiller of the soil."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "India"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d727fbe0-3c53-4ffd-9872-5960b3a9b804",
                                                "sense_id": "0b6d0ae8-67e8-3b0a-9439-1b02e8aa8030",
                                                "text": "We have seen, however, how the condition arose, namely, that the Government at first half-intended to make a permanent settlement direct with the ryots, but subsequently altered its intention and devolved this duty upon the zemindars."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d0fbbdd6-c7ad-47b3-9d0a-7bd34cb6ea1e",
                                                "sense_id": "0b6d0ae8-67e8-3b0a-9439-1b02e8aa8030",
                                                "text": "Scattered about the grazing and arable country are now small towers of refuge, loop-holed for defense, to which ryots working in the fields, or shepherds tending their flocks, fled for safety in case of a sudden appearance of Turcoman marauders."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25072043-740f-4c57-9b8b-cc529eb628aa",
                                                "sense_id": "0b6d0ae8-67e8-3b0a-9439-1b02e8aa8030",
                                                "text": "They are simply the rank and file — the food for fever — sharing with the ryot and the plough-bullock the honor of being the plinth on which the State rests."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
